id:                     E6401
trigger_tool:           Conan|CI|network|PowerShell
phase:                  source-download|conan-create|ci-repair
error_signature:        test-framework GitHub archive timeout after CI mirror predownload; direct recipe download bypasses mirror transform
severity:               2
category:               build,network,conan,evidence
match_keywords:         conan.tools.files.download, test_framework, source_url, gh-proxy.com, GitHub timeout, sha256, partial download cleanup, mirror fallback
title:                  Conan recipe downloads need a bounded hash-verified mirror fallback

root_cause:             A CI wrapper may rewrite conandata.yml for predownload and restore the official bytes before conan create. A recipe-level download() call then consumes the restored single URL directly, so the wrapper's mirror list does not protect test-framework or other auxiliary inputs. When the worker cannot reach github.com, source() fails before compilation even though an approved mirror serves byte-identical content. Treating a non-empty response as success would permit HTML or truncated data to enter the package cache.
affected_scope:        Conan recipes that download auxiliary test sources, wrap files, or other inputs inside source(), especially when the surrounding CI mirror transform is intentionally disposable.
verification_cmd:      Download each candidate into the same destination with the declared SHA-256; delete only a regular partial destination after a failed candidate; require the production source() path to succeed and preserve the official URL in conandata.yml.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           bounded-source-mirror-fallback
rec_description:        Keep the official URL and expected digest as the canonical provenance. For GitHub inputs, try the CI-approved gh-proxy.com prefix once through the normal Conan downloader, then try the official URL. On every exception remove only a regular destination file, retain all errors, and fail closed when no candidate passes the same SHA-256 check.
rec_command:            conan create <recipe> -pr:h <ohos-profile> -pr:b default --build=<package> with source() download fallback
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-level bounded candidate loop around conan.tools.files.download

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      wrapper-only-mirror-rewrite
fallback_description:   CI-side URL rewriting can remain useful for primary source archives, but it cannot cover recipe-level download() calls after the wrapper restores conandata.yml. Use it only when the exact transformed URL list and restore contract are observed.
fallback_command:       inspect conandata.yml.orig and CI predownload log; do not infer auxiliary-input coverage from the wrapper message
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          CI wrapper diagnostic

forbid_1_pattern:       accept first mirror response without sha256|skip digest after fallback|leave partial destination
forbid_1_reason:        A proxy can return an error page or truncated archive while retaining HTTP success and a non-zero size.
forbid_1_consequence:   The build consumes an unverified test framework and may fail later or produce non-reproducible evidence.
forbid_2_pattern:       replace official conandata URL with an unverified personal mirror
forbid_2_reason:        Provenance and future mirror behavior become opaque, and CI may reject the source contract.
forbid_2_consequence:   The candidate loses reproducible source identity even if one local download succeeds.

principles:             P005,P010,P013
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

